# .cursorrules — AeroTerra H2 Aerospace Engineering Project

# ==============================================================================
# 1. GIT & GITHUB AUTOMATION WORKFLOW
# ==============================================================================
# Always ensure clean, atomic, descriptive Git commits following Conventional Commits:
# feat(3d): add CATIA V5 zebra shader surface analysis
# fix(aero): correct Oswald efficiency factor calculation
# perf(webgl): optimize draw calls and buffer geometry allocation
# docs(readme): update flight performance envelope and STOL specs

# Automated Git Push Rules:
# Whenever a major feature or bugfix is completed and verified:
# 1. Run git status to verify modified/created files.
# 2. Stage changes: git add .
# 3. Create descriptive commit: git commit -m "feat(scope): concise description"
# 4. Push directly to remote repository: git push origin main (or active branch)
# 5. Never push broken code or code with console syntax errors.

# ==============================================================================
# 2. CODE QUALITY & ARCHITECTURE STANDARDS
# ==============================================================================
# - Keep application strictly zero-dependency bundlerless (pure HTML5, CSS3, Vanilla JS).
# - Do not add npm build scripts or webpack/vite unless explicitly instructed by the user.
# - Ensure index.html opens and runs immediately in any modern browser via file:// or static server.
# - Maintain 60 FPS in Three.js render loop:
#   * Reuse materials and geometries where possible.
#   * Dispose of unused textures and buffer geometries.
#   * Avoid memory leaks inside requestAnimationFrame.
# - Support dual languages (Russian and English) through the I18N dictionary in app.js.
# - All interactive cards must feature subtle 3D tilt effects with Vanilla-Tilt.
# - Follow aerospace engineering conventions: SI units (kg, m, m/s, km/h, Bar, kW), standard ISA atmosphere.
